
  # CodeMirror Prompt System v2 Backend Integration

  ## Summary

  Implement the v2 intelligence flow in the backend only. The extension remains out of scope except that the
  backend will continue requiring code, leetcode_session, and leetcode_csrf where already defined.

  ## Key Changes

  - Replace current Groq prompt constants with v2 schemas: analyze, pattern_signal_update, pattern_aggregation,
    revision_plan, notification, and coach context.
  - Fix prompt imports so app/prompts/__init__.py no longer imports deleted templates.py.
  - Keep using Submission.code_snapshot as the stored submitted code; do not add a separate code DB column
    unless the API schema changes later.
  - Derive failure_category, severity, root_cause, and code_evidence from Submission.ai_analysis; do not
    reference nonexistent Submission.failure_category or Submission.severity columns.

  ## Implementation Changes

  - Submission analysis:
      - Pass real submitted code into SUBMISSION_ANALYSIS_PROMPT as {code} truncated to 3000 chars.
      - Include existing pattern tags from Pattern.tag.
      - Ensure empty Groq responses fall back to a schema-valid "other" analysis instead of breaking response
        validation.
  - Pattern signal:
      - After storing ai_analysis, call PATTERN_SIGNAL_PROMPT against existing patterns.
      - Store the matched tag in submission.ai_analysis["pattern_signal"].
      - If matched, create/update the SubmissionTag primary link and set the revision queue item’s
        linked_pattern_id.
  - Pattern aggregation:
      - Replace the broken top_patterns aggregation with category grouping over failed submissions from the
        last 30 days using ai_analysis.
      - Trigger after every 3rd failed submission per user.
      - For each category with at least 2 failures, call PATTERN_AGGREGATION_PROMPT, upsert Pattern by
        (user_id, tag), and backfill RevisionQueueItem.linked_pattern_id.
  - Revision plan:
      - Replace hardcoded "Focus on consistency" plan with REVISION_PLAN_PROMPT.
      - Build due item JSON, active pattern summary, and last failure per slug from existing tables.
      - If Groq is unavailable, return a deterministic fallback using real root_cause where available.
  - Coach and notifications:
      - Update /chat to use COACH_SYSTEM_PROMPT plus COACH_CONTEXT_TEMPLATE built from Pattern, Submission, and
        due revision data.
      - Update /notifications/unread to use NOTIFICATION_PROMPT with overdue_slug, forcing cta_route to /
        problems/{slug}.
  - LeetCode sync:
      - Keep /auth/leetcode-session storing actual cookie values.
      - Keep /sync/problems reading snapshots, but make the plan backend-only; extension cookie attachment is
        assumed to be handled separately.

  ## Tests

  - Add/update submission tests to assert code_evidence can come from submitted code_snapshot and response
    populated when a pattern matches.
  - Add notification test confirming cta_route uses problem slug, not title.
    referencing nonexistent submission columns.

  ## Assumptions

  - Backend-only scope, per selection.
  - Existing dirty worktree changes must be preserved; implementation should not restore deleted legacy files
    or revert dashboard changes.
  - PatternImpact remains low | medium | high | critical; v2 prompt impact values map directly except no
    critical is generated by the prompt.
  - Redis caching for revision plans is optional unless an existing Redis client is already wired;
    deterministic DB-backed behavior is required first.